        {
          "id": "01abf354-73c9-3b63-b6bf-fbc2d0da076a",
          "content": {
            "id": "01abf354-73c9-3b63-b6bf-fbc2d0da076a",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "BMW shares drop after profit forecast cut on tariffs, China weakness",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: BMW shares took a wrong turn on Wednesday as they fell just under a tenth in early trade.</p><p>Investors sold off after the German carmaker cut its earnings forecast for this year.</p><p>It blamed changed U.S. tariff assumptions and weaker-than-expected growth in the Chinese market.</p><p>The company narrowed its profit forecast to 5-6% in its cars business from the 5-7% range it had previously predicted.</p><p>BMW further warned pre-tax earnings are now likely to fall slightly this year.</p><p>The automaker also halved expectations for the automotive segment's free cash flow to above $2.9 billion.</p><p>It cited delays to refunds from U.S. customs.</p><p>BMW and its European rivals have had setbacks in China due to strong local competition and a real-estate downturn.</p><p>BMW did record sales growth in Europe and America through the end of September.</p><p>But it said the targeted sales increase in China was below expectations.</p><p>Local rival Mercedes also saw shares fall on Wednesday.</p><p>It reported falling sales on U.S. import duties and stronger competition in China.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: BMW shares took a wrong turn on Wednesday as they fell just under a tenth in early trade.</p><p>Investors sold off after the German carmaker cut its earnings forecast for this year.</p><p>It blamed changed U.S. tariff assumptions and weaker-than-expected growth in the Chinese market.</p><p>The company narrowed its profit forecast to 5-6% in its cars business from the 5-7% range it had previously predicted.</p><p>BMW further warned pre-tax earnings are now likely to fall slightly this year.</p><p>The automaker also halved expectations for the automotive segment's free cash flow to above $2.9 billion.</p><p>It cited delays to refunds from U.S. customs.</p><p>BMW and its European rivals have had setbacks in China due to strong local competition and a real-estate downturn.</p><p>BMW did record sales growth in Europe and America through the end of September.</p><p>But it said the targeted sales increase in China was below expectations.</p><p>Local rival Mercedes also saw shares fall on Wednesday.</p><p>It reported falling sales on U.S. import duties and stronger competition in China.</p></body>",
